t would be their business. The neighbors could have charged the players with a crime, called the team and asked them to step in, demanded money or punish the team in other ways. No one is saying that they did not have a right to do that. The people who decide are called citizens. They have a right to decide who works for whom, and how well. Yet, in the real world, there are limits. The law is the limit. ## Public Shame And Rush To Punishment The second problem is the media. Their job is to let us know what is happening in the world. They are not just giving their opinion on a matter. They also report what is happening. In this case, they are not talking about a matter. They are not even reporting about what is happening. People cannot judge a case for themselves. There are rules that cannot be broken. They are not called rules. They are called laws. They are rules of the land which everyone is to follow. If the laws are not followed, then there must be punishment. It should never happen that a group of people are punished for a crime that they have not been convicted of. Punishing a group of people after a crime has happened is wrong, no matter who has been punished. Those of us in America are lucky enough to live in a great country. We have a justice system. It is there to decide in a fair way whether a person has been accused of a crime. Once the crime has happened, people ought to be punished. They should be punished the way the law says they should. That is the right thing. ## Fair Trials Should Be Held Even More And if we are to stop this trend of rushing to punish without having a trial, we must go back decades to the time of Thomas Jefferson. Jefferson was one of the greatest leaders in America. He helped write the Declaration of Independence, which changed America forever. Jefferson was the nation's third president. Jefferson lived from 1743 until 1826. Jefferson lived 82 years and 15 days. 243 people died in office while Jefferson was alive. For a period, Jefferson served as one of America's two top leaders, President of the Senate. There is another famous American leader, who also lived in Jefferson's time. He lived from 1812 until 1899. It is President George Washington. Washington lived 87 years and 4 days. Then he died. ## Jefferson Was A Good Writer Washington was 80 years old when he died. Washington died before Jefferson, and he was nearly 60 when Jefferson died. Washington was the nation's first president. Washington died at age 80. Jefferson died 91 years later, when he was 82. Jefferson lived 82 years, and Washington lived 87. Jefferson was 8 years older than Washington. That means it is not even possible that Jefferson is younger than Washington. We can assume that Jefferson is the older. Jefferson lives about 17-18 years longer than Washington's 87 years. Yet Jefferson was also president for a shorter period than Washington's 80 years. Jefferson lived nearly 61 years as president. Washington lived 80 years. Jefferson was president for one term each. Washington was president twice. Washington had 4 years as president. Jefferson had 6 years as president. ## It's An American System The point I'm trying to make is that all leaders have different lengths. Jefferson was president for a shorter time than George Washington. They also had different leadership styles. Yet, they both lived nearly the same number of years. Jefferson was 82 years old at death. Washington was 80 years old at death. We are lucky to live in a democracy. We are lucky to have a system of justice. The justice system makes sure that nobody can be punished for a crime without a trial. Jefferson lived 82 years, and Washington died 87 years. Yet they both lived nearly the same number of years. It is wrong for us to punish people without a trial. After the 2014 congressional elections, there will be changes at the top in Washington. New members of Congress will be elected. It will be a new day with new ideas, new ideas about our business at Washington, D.C. There will be new ideas about what we are going to do as a nation. If the new leaders in Washington say what they are looking for is a way to make things fair again, they will be right. It is the American system that way. 
